** Probe: the single-urban-area forms of URBANOPT and URBANSRC.
** First guesses, from pyaermod's own writer, were "URBANOPT name pop"
** and "URBANSRC srcid name". AERMOD said E208 (URBOPT: Illegal Numerical
** Field in URB-POP) and E300 (URBANS: Specified SRCID Has Not Been
** Defined Yet): with one URBANOPT card the first field is the
** population and every URBANSRC field is a source ID (coset.f URBOPT,
** soset.f URBANS with ISTR=3). The id-first forms are only read when
** the deck has several URBANOPT cards (L_MULTURB).
CO STARTING
   TITLEONE  oracle 13: URBANOPT population [name] [z0]; URBANSRC ids
   MODELOPT  CONC  FLAT  DFAULT
   AVERTIME  1
   POLLUTID  SO2
   URBANOPT  700000.  INDIANAPOLIS
   RUNORNOT  NOT
CO FINISHED

SO STARTING
   LOCATION  STACK1  POINT  0.0  0.0  0.0
   SRCPARAM  STACK1  500.0  65.00  425.  15.0  5.
   LOCATION  STACK2  POINT  50.0  0.0  0.0
   SRCPARAM  STACK2  500.0  65.00  425.  15.0  5.
   URBANSRC  STACK1  STACK2
   SRCGROUP  ALL
SO FINISHED

RE STARTING
   DISCCART  500.0  500.0  0.0
RE FINISHED

ME STARTING
   SURFFILE  AERMET2.SFC
   PROFFILE  AERMET2.PFL
   SURFDATA  14735  1988
   UAIRDATA  14735  1988
   PROFBASE  0.0  METERS
ME FINISHED

OU STARTING
